    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49654" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ulpius</span></b> , i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a
			Roman</i> gens. So esp., M. Ulpius Trajanus, <i>the
				celebrated Roman emperor of that name.</i>—Hence, 
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ulpĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Ulpius</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">porticus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 8, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
